## Control {{controlId}}: Prevent Non-Privileged Users from Executing Privileged Functions

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization prevents non-privileged users from executing privileged functions within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Privileged function restriction is enforced through Azure AD role-based access control, Conditional Access policies, and Privileged Identity Management (PIM) approval workflows that block unauthorized elevation of privileges.

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
Conditional Access policies enforce privileged function restrictions across {{caPoliciesTotalCount}} configured policies. Non-privileged users attempting to access administrative portals (Azure Portal, Microsoft 365 Admin Center, Exchange Admin Center) are blocked by policies requiring privileged role membership and compliant device authentication.
{{else}}
Conditional Access policies restricting privileged function execution have not been configured. Privileged function access relies on Azure AD role assignment only, pending Conditional Access enforcement.
{{/if}}

{{#if pimConfigured}}
Privileged Identity Management requires approval workflows for all privileged role activations. Non-privileged users cannot self-elevate to administrative roles without explicit approval from a designated administrator, creating an auditable authorization chain.
{{/if}}

{{#if signInLogsAvailable}}
Sign-in logs capture {{signInLogsCount}} authentication events for monitoring unauthorized privilege escalation attempts. Failed elevation attempts trigger security alerts reviewed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.
{{/if}}

